{"id":"mahabharata-13-054","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":54,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 54 · The forest of wonders","summary":{"en":"The king goes at dawn with his wife to the lovely forest and hears sweet song and the sound of study and sees swans. He marvels at the power of the sage Chyavana, who by his austerity could make other worlds, and asks him to resolve a doubt.","kn":"ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ ರಾಜ ಪತ್ನಿಯೊಡನೆ ಸುಂದರ ವನಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗಿ ಮಧುರ ಗೀತ, ವೇದಾಧ್ಯಯನ ಧ್ವನಿ, ಹಂಸಗಳನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಬೇರೆ ಲೋಕಗಳನ್ನೇ ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಸಬಲ್ಲ ಚ್ಯವನನ ಶಕ್ತಿಗೆ ಬೆರಗಾಗಿ ತನ್ನ ಸಂಶಯ ಬಗೆಹರಿಸಲು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"प्रातः राजा पत्नी सहित सुन्दर वन जाता है और मधुर गीत, अध्ययन की ध्वनि और हंस देखता-सुनता है। वह तप से अन्य लोक रच सकने वाले च्यवन की शक्ति पर चकित होकर अपना संशय दूर करने को कहता है।","te":"ఉదయం రాజు భార్యతో అందమైన వనానికి వెళ్లి మధుర గీతం, అధ్యయన ధ్వని, హంసలను చూస్తాడు. తపస్సుతో ఇతర లోకాలనే సృష్టించగల చ్యవనుని శక్తికి ఆశ్చర్యపడి తన సందేహం తీర్చమని అడుగుతాడు.","ta":"விடியலில் மன்னன் மனைவியுடன் அழகிய காட்டுக்குச் சென்று இனிய பாடல், ஓதும் ஒலி, அன்னப் பறவைகளைக் காண்கிறான். தவத்தால் வேறு உலகங்களையே படைக்கக்கூடிய சியவனரின் ஆற்றலை வியந்து தன் ஐயத்தைத் தீர்க்கக் கேட்கிறான்.","ml":"പുലർച്ചെ രാജാവ് രാജ്ഞിയോടൊപ്പം മനോഹരമായ വനത്തിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു; മധുരമായ പാട്ടും പഠനത്തിന്റെ ശബ്ദവും കേൾക്കുന്നു, ഹംസങ്ങളെ കാണുന്നു. തപസ്സുകൊണ്ട് മറ്റു ലോകങ്ങൾ സൃഷ്ടിക്കാൻ കഴിയുന്ന ച്യവനമുനിയുടെ ശക്തിയിൽ അദ്ദേഹം അത്ഭുതപ്പെടുന്നു; ഒരു സംശയം പരിഹരിക്കണമെന്ന് മുനിയോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.54; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः स राजा रात्र्यन्ते प्रतिबुद्धो महामनाः ।\nकृतपूर्वाह्णिकः प्रायात्सभार्यस्तद्वनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At night's end that great-minded king woke, performed his morning rites, and went with his wife toward that forest."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो ददर्श नृपतिः प्रासादं सर्वकाञ्चनम् ।\nमणिस्तम्भसहस्राढ्यं गन्धर्वनगरोपमम् ।\nतत्र दिव्यानभिप्रायान्ददर्श कुशिकस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king saw a palace wholly of gold, rich with thousands of jewelled pillars, like a city of gandharvas; and there Kushika saw divine wonders."}},{"n":3,"text":"पर्वतान्रम्यसानूंश्च नलिनीश्च सपङ्कजाः ।\nचित्रशालाश्च विविधास्तोरणानि च भारत ।\nशाद्वलोपचितां भूमिं तथा काञ्चनकुट्टिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw mountains with lovely slopes, lotus ponds with blossoms, many painting halls and archways, O Bharata, and ground covered with grass and paved with gold."}},{"n":4,"text":"सहकारान्प्रफुल्लांश्च केतकोद्दालकान्धवान् ।\nअशोकान्मुचुकुन्दांश्च फुल्लांश्चैवातिमुक्तकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there he saw flowering mango trees, ketaka, uddalaka and dhava trees, ashoka, muchukunda, and blossoming atimuktaka creepers,"}},{"n":5,"text":"चम्पकांस्तिलकान्भव्यान्पनसान्वञ्जुलानपि ।\nपुष्पितान्कर्णिकारांश्च तत्र तत्र ददर्श ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"champaka, handsome tilaka, jackfruit, vanjula, and blooming karnikara trees."}},{"n":6,"text":"श्यामां वारणपुष्पीं च तथाष्टापदिकां लताम् ।\nतत्र तत्र परिकॢप्ता ददर्श स महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king also saw dark shyama creepers, varanapushpi, and the ashtapadika vine, arranged in various places."}},{"n":7,"text":"वृक्षान्पद्मोत्पलधरान्सर्वर्तुकुसुमांस्तथा ।\nविमानच्छन्दकांश्चापि प्रासादान्पद्मसंनिभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw trees bearing lotuses and water lilies, flowering in every season, mansions shaped like aerial cars, and palaces like lotuses."}},{"n":8,"text":"शीतलानि च तोयानि क्वचिदुष्णानि भारत ।\nआसनानि विचित्राणि शयनप्रवराणि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was cool water and, in places, warm water, O Bharata, with varied seats and excellent beds,"}},{"n":9,"text":"पर्यङ्कान्सर्वसौवर्णान्परार्ध्यास्तरणास्तृतान् ।\nभक्ष्यभोज्यमनन्तं च तत्र तत्रोपकल्पितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"couches wholly of gold spread with costly covers, and endless food and drink provided here and there."}},{"n":10,"text":"वाणीवादाञ्छुकांश्चापि शारिकाभृङ्गराजकान् ।\nकोकिलाञ्छतपत्रांश्च कोयष्टिमककुक्कुटान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw talking parrots, mynas, bhringarajas, cuckoos, shatapatras, koyashtis, and wild cocks,"}},{"n":11,"text":"मयूरान्कुक्कुटांश्चापि पुत्रकाञ्जीवजीवकान् ।\nचकोरान्वानरान्हंसान्सारसांश्चक्रसाह्वयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"peacocks, hens, putrakas, jivajivakas, chakoras, monkeys, swans, cranes and chakravaka birds,"}},{"n":12,"text":"समन्ततः प्रणदितान्ददर्श सुमनोहरान् ।\nक्वचिदप्सरसां संघान्गन्धर्वाणां च पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"all around, making very charming sounds; and in places he saw troops of apsaras and of gandharvas, O king."}},{"n":13,"text":"कान्ताभिरपरांस्तत्र परिष्वक्तान्ददर्श ह ।\nन ददर्श च तान्भूयो ददर्श च पुनर्नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others he saw there embraced by their beloved women; the king would no longer see them, and then see them again."}},{"n":14,"text":"गीतध्वनिं सुमधुरं तथैवाध्ययनध्वनिम् ।\nहंसान्सुमधुरांश्चापि तत्र शुश्राव पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king heard sweet singing, the sound of Vedic recitation, and the very sweet notes of swans."}},{"n":15,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वात्यद्भुतं राजा मनसाचिन्तयत्तदा ।\nस्वप्नोऽयं चित्तविभ्रंश उताहो सत्यमेव तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that great marvel, the king wondered in his mind, \"Is this a dream, a delusion of the mind, or truly real?"}},{"n":16,"text":"अहो सह शरीरेण प्राप्तोऽस्मि परमां गतिम् ।\nउत्तरान्वा कुरून्पुण्यानथ वाप्यमरावतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ah, have I reached the highest state with my body, or the holy Northern Kurus, or Amaravati?"}},{"n":17,"text":"किं त्विदं महदाश्चर्यं संपश्यामीत्यचिन्तयत् ।\nएवं संचिन्तयन्नेव ददर्श मुनिपुंगवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is this great wonder that I see?\" he thought. While he was thinking thus, he saw the best of sages,"}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्मिन्विमाने सौवर्णे मणिस्तम्भसमाकुले ।\nमहार्हे शयने दिव्ये शयानं भृगुनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the son of Bhrigu, lying on a costly divine bed in that golden aerial palace crowded with jewelled pillars."}},{"n":19,"text":"तमभ्ययात्प्रहर्षेण नरेन्द्रः सह भार्यया ।\nअन्तर्हितस्ततो भूयश्च्यवनः शयनं च तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king went toward him with his wife in great joy; but then Chyavana and that bed vanished again."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततोऽन्यस्मिन्वनोद्देशे पुनरेव ददर्श तम् ।\nकौश्यां बृस्यां समासीनं जपमानं महाव्रतम् ।\nएवं योगबलाद्विप्रो मोहयामास पार्थिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in another part of the forest he saw him again, seated on a mat of kusha grass, muttering prayers, firm in great vows. Thus by the power of yoga the brahmin bewildered the king."}},{"n":21,"text":"क्षणेन तद्वनं चैव ते चैवाप्सरसां गणाः ।\nगन्धर्वाः पादपाश्चैव सर्वमन्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In an instant that forest, those troops of apsaras, the gandharvas and the trees, everything vanished."}},{"n":22,"text":"निःशब्दमभवच्चापि गङ्गाकूलं पुनर्नृप ।\nकुशवल्मीकभूयिष्ठं बभूव च यथा पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bank of the Ganga became silent again, O king, and was thick with kusha grass and anthills as before."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः स राजा कुशिकः सभार्यस्तेन कर्मणा ।\nविस्मयं परमं प्राप्तस्तद्दृष्ट्वा महदद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Kushika with his wife, having seen that great marvel wrought, fell into supreme astonishment."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः प्रोवाच कुशिको भार्यां हर्षसमन्वितः ।\nपश्य भद्रे यथा भावाश्चित्रा दृष्टाः सुदुर्लभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kushika, filled with joy, said to his wife, \"Look, good lady, what rare and wondrous visions we have seen."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रसादाद्भृगुमुख्यस्य किमन्यत्र तपोबलात् ।\nतपसा तदवाप्यं हि यन्न शक्यं मनोरथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the grace of the foremost Bhrigu, what else is there but the power of austerity? By austerity one can obtain what cannot be had by mere wishes."}},{"n":26,"text":"त्रैलोक्यराज्यादपि हि तप एव विशिष्यते ।\nतपसा हि सुतप्तेन क्रीडत्येष तपोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even above rule over the three worlds, austerity is the better thing; for this wealth of austerity plays at will through well-practised penance."}},{"n":27,"text":"अहो प्रभावो ब्रह्मर्षेश्च्यवनस्य महात्मनः ।\nइच्छन्नेष तपोवीर्यादन्याँल्लोकान्सृजेदपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ah, the power of the great-souled Chyavana, the brahmin sage! If he wished, by the strength of his austerity he could create other worlds as well."}},{"n":28,"text":"ब्राह्मणा एव जायेरन्पुण्यवाग्बुद्धिकर्मणः ।\nउत्सहेदिह कर्तुं हि कोऽन्यो वै च्यवनादृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins alone might be born with holy speech, thought and deeds; who else here would dare to do this, except Chyavana?"}},{"n":29,"text":"ब्राह्मण्यं दुर्लभं लोके राज्यं हि सुलभं नरैः ।\nब्राह्मण्यस्य प्रभावाद्धि रथे युक्तौ स्वधुर्यवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahminhood is rare in the world, while kingship is easily gained by men; it is through the power of brahminhood that we two were yoked to the chariot like draught animals.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"इत्येवं चिन्तयानः स विदितश्च्यवनस्य वै ।\nसंप्रेक्ष्योवाच स नृपं क्षिप्रमागम्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he thought thus, Chyavana, who knew it, looked at him and said to the king, \"Come quickly.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"इत्युक्तः सहभार्यस्तमभ्यगच्छन्महामुनिम् ।\nशिरसा वन्दनीयं तमवन्दत स पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So told, he went with his wife to the great sage, and the king bowed his head to him, who deserved reverence."}},{"n":32,"text":"तस्याशिषः प्रयुज्याथ स मुनिस्तं नराधिपम् ।\nनिषीदेत्यब्रवीद्धीमान्सान्त्वयन्पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage blessed him and, soothing him, said to the king, \"Sit down,\" O best of men."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततः प्रकृतिमापन्नो भार्गवो नृपते नृपम् ।\nउवाच श्लक्ष्णया वाचा तर्पयन्निव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhargava, having returned to his natural self, spoke to the king in a gentle voice, as if gratifying him, O Bharata."}},{"n":34,"text":"राजन्सम्यग्जितानीह पञ्च पञ्चसु यत्त्वया ।\nमनःषष्ठानीन्द्रियाणि कृच्छ्रान्मुक्तोऽसि तेन वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King, you have rightly conquered the five in the five, and the senses with the mind as sixth; by that you are freed from hardship."}},{"n":35,"text":"सम्यगाराधितः पुत्र त्वयाहं वदतां वर ।\nन हि ते वृजिनं किंचित्सुसूक्ष्ममपि विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, best of speakers, I have been well served by you; there is no fault in you, not even a very tiny one."}},{"n":36,"text":"अनुजानीहि मां राजन्गमिष्यामि यथागतम् ।\nप्रीतोऽस्मि तव राजेन्द्र वरश्च प्रतिगृह्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give me leave, king; I will go as I came. I am pleased with you, king of kings; accept a boon.\""}},{"text":"कुशिक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kushika said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"अग्निमध्यगतेनेदं भगवन्संनिधौ मया ।\nवर्तितं भृगुशार्दूल यन्न दग्धोऽस्मि तद्बहु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lord, that I was kept in your presence as if in the midst of fire, and was not burned, is a great thing, tiger of Bhrigu's line."}},{"n":38,"text":"एष एव वरो मुख्यः प्राप्तो मे भृगुनन्दन ।\nयत्प्रीतोऽसि समाचारात्कुलं पूतं ममानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is itself the chief boon I have gained, son of Bhrigu: that you are pleased with my conduct and that my family is purified, blameless one."}},{"n":39,"text":"एष मेऽनुग्रहो विप्र जीविते च प्रयोजनम् ।\nएतद्राज्यफलं चैव तपश्चैतत्परं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is your favour, brahmin, and the purpose of my life; this is the fruit of my kingdom, and this is my highest austerity."}},{"n":40,"text":"यदि तु प्रीतिमान्विप्र मयि त्वं भृगुनन्दन ।\nअस्ति मे संशयः कश्चित्तन्मे व्याख्यातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if you are pleased with me, brahmin, son of Bhrigu, I have a doubt; you should explain it to me.\""}}]}]}